WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.748
Recovery restores trusted operations after containment and eradication have reduced the risk to an acceptable level.

00:00:05.748 --> 00:00:09.279
Recovery may include rebuilding systems, restoring from backups, re-enabling services,

00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:12.103
validating patches, checking data integrity, reviewing account state,

00:00:12.103 --> 00:00:13.515
and monitoring for recurrence.

00:00:13.515 --> 00:00:15.633
The phrase trusted operations is important.

00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:19.870
Recovery should not mean turning everything back on as quickly as possible

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.988
and hoping the issue is gone.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:26.577
It means the organization has enough evidence that systems are safe to operate,

00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:30.107
controls are working, and business owners understand any residual risk.

00:00:30.107 --> 00:00:31.519
Recovery is usually coordinated,

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:35.403
because technical readiness and business readiness are not always the same.

00:00:35.403 --> 00:00:38.933
A system owner may confirm that a server is rebuilt,

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:42.463
while a business owner confirms that a process can resume.

00:00:42.463 --> 00:00:47.406
Monitoring should continue after recovery because some issues reappear only after normal traffic returns.

00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:51.995
Communication also matters: stakeholders need to know what is restored, what remains limited,

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:55.878
what users should expect, and when the next update will come.

00:00:55.878 --> 00:01:01.527
Good recovery closes the immediate incident while keeping watch for signs that more work is needed.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.998
Recovery should include a deliberate observation period.

00:01:03.998 --> 00:01:07.881
After service is restored, responders should keep watching relevant logs, alerts,

00:01:07.881 --> 00:01:09.646
account behavior, and business signals.

00:01:09.646 --> 00:01:13.883
That follow-up monitoring helps confirm that eradication worked and gives stakeholders confidence

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:17.060
that normal operations are returning for the right reasons.
